@@ -72,17 +72,35 @@
 
 ## Connect a real Firebase project
 
+Margin uses **Firebase AI Logic** for hybrid inference, **App Check** to attest requests, and **Remote Config** for routing settings. The optional backup uses **Firebase Authentication** and **Cloud Firestore**.
+
 1. Create a Firebase project and add a **Web app** in **Project settings**. In **AI Services → AI Logic**, select **Get started**, choose **Gemini Developer API**, and finish enabling the required services. [Firebase AI Logic setup](https://firebase.google.com/docs/ai-logic/get-started?platform=web)
 2. Copy `firebase.config.example.json` to `firebase.config.local.json`. Paste the values from the Firebase web app configuration into that JSON file. Run `npm run build` and load or reload `dist/`. The local file is ignored by Git. [Firebase web configuration](https://firebase.google.com/docs/web/learn-more#config-object)
 3. Open the side panel or Options and inspect that extension page with Chrome DevTools. Find the **Firebase App Check debug token** logged on initialization. In Firebase Console, open **App Check → Apps**, find the web app, choose **Manage debug tokens**, and register the value. To use an existing debug token, enter it in Margin **Options → App Check debug token**, save, and reopen the extension pages. Keep debug tokens private. Public distribution with App Check enforcement requires a production attestation provider. [App Check debug provider](https://firebase.google.com/docs/app-check/web/debug-provider)
 4. Use desktop Chrome 139 or newer on a device that supports the Prompt API. Enable `chrome://flags/#prompt-api-for-gemini-nano-multimodal-input`, restart Chrome, and click **Enable on-device AI** in the side panel when offered. Wait for **On-device ready**. [Firebase hybrid setup and Chrome requirements](https://firebase.google.com/docs/ai-logic/hybrid/web/get-started)
-5. In Margin Options, turn off **Demo mode** and select **Auto router**. Generate from a short passage to check the on-device badge, then select **Only cloud** and use nonsensitive notes to check the cloud badge. Return to Auto afterward.
+5. In Margin Options, turn off **Demo mode**, select **Auto router**, and run the live test under **Diagnostics**. To verify the cloud route explicitly, select **Only cloud** and generate from nonsensitive notes. Return to Auto afterward.
 6. Optionally publish Firebase Remote Config values for `maxOnDeviceTokens`, `cloudModel`, `longDocModel`, `sensitivityCheck`, and `maxCardsPerChunk`. Set the cloud model names to models available to your Firebase project.
 
 ## Demo mode
 
 Without Firebase configuration, Margin uses a deterministic simulation for generation, routing, and answer feedback. A **DEMO MODE (simulated AI)** banner identifies every extension page in that mode. Options can enable the simulation on a configured build, and `MOCK=1 npm run build` forces it for the built extension. Demo generation and grading work without Firebase credentials.
 
+## Diagnostics
+
+Open **Options → Diagnostics** to check the Chrome version, Prompt API, current `LanguageModel.availability()` result, Firebase configuration, App Check, Remote Config values, and Demo or Live mode. If App Check cannot obtain a token, register the debug token from DevTools in Firebase Console and reopen Options.
+
+**Run live hybrid test** sends one built-in prompt through Firebase AI Logic with `PREFER_ON_DEVICE`. The result shows the returned `inferenceSource` (`on_device` or `in_cloud`) and inference latency. The prompt contains no library or captured content. Live mode and a configured Firebase project are required. [Firebase hybrid inference options](https://firebase.google.com/docs/ai-logic/hybrid/web/configuration-options)
+
+## Firestore backup
+
+1. In the same Firebase project, enable the **Anonymous** sign-in provider under **Authentication → Sign-in method**. [Anonymous Authentication setup](https://firebase.google.com/docs/auth/web/anonymous-auth)
+2. Create a Cloud Firestore database and publish [firestore.rules](firestore.rules) in its **Rules** tab. The rules limit access under each user path to that user's authenticated UID. [Firestore Security Rules](https://firebase.google.com/docs/firestore/security/rules-conditions)
+3. In **Options → Firestore backup**, turn on **Back up decks to Firestore**. Margin signs in anonymously and backs up the library when enabled and after local card or deck changes. Use **Back up now** to retry. Backup and restore are paused in Demo mode and Privacy mode.
+
+Firestore stores decks under `users/{uid}/decks/{deckId}` and cards under `users/{uid}/cards/{cardId}`. Card documents contain the front, back, tags, deck ID, card type, creation time, and FSRS schedule. Captured source text, source links, routing history, and review logs stay out of the backup.
+
+**Restore from backup** adds missing decks and cards while preserving local copies with matching IDs. Local deletions remain in existing backups and can reappear on restore. The anonymous account is tied to this Chrome profile and extension ID. Clearing its extension data or switching profiles can leave the backup inaccessible.
+
 ## Scripts
 
 Use Node.js 24 LTS (24.15 or newer) and install Playwright Chromium with `npx playwright install chromium`. On Linux CI, `npx playwright install --with-deps chromium` also installs browser system dependencies.
@@ -109,7 +127,7 @@
 
 ## Privacy
 
-Cards, route history, queued source material, and review history live in this Chrome profile. On-device generation and typed-answer grading keep their input on the device. Cloud routes send the selected source content or media to Firebase AI Logic and the Gemini API. In Privacy mode, no source content leaves your machine. When Firebase is configured and Demo mode is off, Margin still fetches routing settings from Firebase Remote Config. Margin uses temporary Chrome tab access for captures and requests access to a particular site when a page or PDF needs additional permission. You can manage granted site access in Chrome’s extension settings.
+Cards, route history, queued source material, and review history live in this Chrome profile. On-device generation and typed-answer grading keep their input on the device. Cloud routes send the selected source content or media to Firebase AI Logic and the Gemini API. Firestore backup is off by default. In Privacy mode, Margin keeps source content on your machine and pauses Firestore backup and restore. When Firebase is configured and Demo mode is off, Margin still fetches routing settings from Firebase Remote Config. Margin uses temporary Chrome tab access for captures and requests access to a particular site when a page or PDF needs additional permission. You can manage granted site access in Chrome’s extension settings.
 
